{"text": "RINGER, HENRY, BUCKLEY & SEACORD, P.A.\nAltrneys at Lane\n\n4105 \u20ac Rosinson Srreer, SumTE 400\nORLANDO, FLORIDA 32801\n\u2018VA RINGERHENRY.COM\n\nREPLY AOORESS!\nPost OFFice Box 4922\nOnuanoo, FL 32802-4922 Roper D. Hen\nTELEPHONE 407-641-3800 |HENRY@RINGERKENRY.COM\n\nFacswwae 407-841-3855\n\nJuly\n\n018\n\nVIA EMAIL: mare@fbswlaw.com\n\nD. Mare Warner, Esq.\nWarmer, Sechrest & Butts, PA.\n5200 SW 91\" Terrace, Suite 101\nGainesville, FL 32608\n\nRE: \u2014 Cudnik v, Reynolds\nDear Mr, Warner:\n\nThis letter follows our recent telephone conversation conceming this matter. As |\nreported to you by telephone, I have spoken to Ms. Reynolds and confirmed that she and the birth\ncenter do not have coverage for this claim. In 2015, Ms. Reynolds was covered by the Lancet,\nInsurance Company. The policy premium to renew that policy in 2016 was excessive, and so she\ncancelled and switched to the Florida Medical Malpractice Joint Underwriting Association. The\npremium for tail coverage for the Lancet was also excessive and she could not afford it\nUnfortunately, the Lancet was a claims-made policy and therefore does not cover this claim\nbecause it came in after the policy expired. The FMMJUA policy is on an occurrence form,\nmeaning that it only covers occurrences which occur during the policy period. I have enclosed an\nAffidavit of Ms. Reynolds with some supporting documentation.\n\nTam trying to assist Ms. Reynolds without making an appearance. Not only does she not\nhave insurance, but she does not have assets that would cover even a small judgment.\n\nYou indicated during our call that you would speak to your client about dismissing the\ncase, Ifyou need additional information or would like to discuss it further, please let me know. I\nlook forward to hearing fom you in the near future. \u2018Thank you for your consideration\n\nSincerely,\n\n4 $-\u2014~\n& >\nRobert D. Henry\n\nEnclosures\nce: Amy Reynolds\n\nLARDHNLT-WARNER-OOL\nRD",
